4. The petitioner as plaintiff instituted Other Suit No.76 of 1989 in the 2nd Court of learned Joint District Judge, Chattogram with, inter alia, the following prayers: — (i) A decree for specific performance of the memorandum of agreement of sale dated 29-5-1983 be passed against defendant No.1 directing defendant No.1 to return and deliver up the fishing trawlers described in schedule 'A' below to the plaintiff. And/or the replacements thereof and in the alternative a decree be passed enabling the plaintiff to get ownership and to retain possession of the Trawler 'SUNGTHON' as described in the schedule below within a specified time; 

 (iv) A decree declaring that defendant No.1 is only entitled to the purchase price of the fishing trawlers as agreed upon between the plaintiff and defendant No.1 pursuant to memorandum of agreement of sale dated 29-5-1983 and the plaintiff is liable to pay the same only upon return and delivery of the said trawlers and/or the replacement thereof to the plaintiff and also upon completing all formalities for sending the said money upon receiving permission from the defendant No.10 and other relevant competent authorities; 

 (vii) A decree declaring that defendant Nos.2 and 3 having committed offences in removing and spiriting away the said fishing trawlers, described in Schedule-A hereto, from the lawful possession of the plaintiff and out of the economic zone/ maritime zone of Bangladesh are liable to be prosecuted by defendant Nos.4-10 and that the said defendant Nos.4-10 may take such proceedings as are appropriate for their prosecution and extradition; 

 (ix) A decree for Taka 36,00,000 as damages and compensation against defendant Nos.1-3 jointly and severally, and in favour of the plaintiff; 

 (xi) A decree for attachment of any property whatsoever of defendant Nos.1-3.
